message.content:
Read-only design task. Edit nothing except writing ONE new temp file at the end. Repository: /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec.

Classify EVERY skill into exactly one category. Skills in repo: skills/{live-spec-base, build-pipeline, spec-author, communicator, text-audit, design-reviewer, test-author, publish, feedback-collector, feedback-intake, product-prover-pack}. Also list (but mark "рантайм, вне репо — только констатация") the installed-only ones: ~/.claude/skills/{product-prover (stale v4.3.0 copy; real canon is an external 1.x repo), skill-creator (Anthropic's), track-coach (other project)}.

Categories:
1. pack-internal router/base — must stay inside the pack;
2. on-demand module/reference — stays but loads only when needed;
3. independent reusable product candidate — could live as its own repo/product (the existing precedent: product-prover was already extracted to an external repo with a thin adapter pack `product-prover-pack` left behind — study that pattern: the pack's SKILL.md, scripts/install-external-skills.sh, conftest/guardrails pins);
4. obsolete/duplicate.

Evidence per skill (keep it quick): frontmatter description/trigger, size, who invokes it (grep other skills + docs for its name), what it depends on (grep its body for live-spec-base rules, repo paths, guardrails). One line of evidence per classification.

For EVERY category-3 candidate, write an extraction PROPOSAL (do not extract anything): ownership (which repo, who versions it), dependency contract (what it needs from a host project, what must be severed from live-spec-base), versioning line, README skeleton (5 bullet outline), tests that travel with it, the thin adapter left in LiveSpec (по образцу product-prover-pack), and migration path (order of steps, what breaks in between, rollback). Be honest about candidates that look reusable but are welded to the pack — put them in category 2 with one line saying what weld blocks category 3.

Write the full result to /private/tmp/live-spec-control/skill-classification.md: a classification table (skill | category | evidence | action) then one proposal section per category-3 candidate (≤20 lines each). Return in your final message ONLY the table and the names of category-3 candidates, plain Russian, ≤25 lines.
